  "course_description": "Scholarly Inquiry and Research at Emory - With joint funding from the Laney Graduate School and the Dean's Office of Emory College of Arts and Sciences,Emory College's Office for Undergraduate Education will award graduate students fellowships to advanced graduate students in the humanities and social sciences.",
  "course_notes": "Scholarly Inquiry and Research Experience (SIRE) prepares students with little to no previous research experience to become active participants in Emory's research community across disciplines. The course introduces students to the structures, practices, and people that make research possible at a research-intensive university and helps them develop the knowledge and professional skills needed to enter faculty-led research responsibly.",
